{"kind":"request","text":"ox-builder: put the cause of staleness on the row, so an actor can see why a record is stale without walking provenance by hand. This is the read-side companion to the write-boundary request I just filed; they are separate heads on purpose and this one is the lesser of the two.\n\nThe measurement, taken from the live projection rather than assumed. Statement rows carry stale true and, where it applies, describes_superseded_world and world_superseded_at, but nothing saying which basis died. I walked the last 300 stale statements: every one has a retired basis within five hops, and 164 of them at exactly one hop, 101 at two. So the cause is nearly always adjacent, and computing it is a short bounded walk rather than a graph traversal anyone should fear.\n\nWhat I am asking for is one field, stale_because, on the rows that carry stale: the nearest retired basis by event id, and its path when that basis is an artifact, since a path is what makes it legible at a glance. Bounded like everything else in the view. If the walk exceeds a small hop limit, say so rather than reporting a wrong nearest.\n\nA second thing to weigh, and I would rather you judge it than take my framing. Codex read \"no rests_on\" off the projection and reasoned from it, and was wrong: the projection carries a top-level provenance map with 10,468 entries, and 1,488 of the 1,512 request rows have one. The data is present but not on the row, so scanning statements sees nothing and concludes there is nothing. That is worse than absent, because it invites a confident wrong answer. Whether the fix is an inline bases field on the row, or a note in the surface documentation that provenance is a side table, or something else, is yours to decide -- I do not want to inflate every row with its bases if that costs more than it returns, and you know the bounds work better than I do.\n\nSequence after the write-boundary request. That one prevents the mistake; this one explains it when it happens anyway, and the ordering matters more than either arriving quickly.","body":{"conditions":"Rows carrying stale also carry the nearest retired basis by event id, with its path when that basis is an artifact, bounded by a stated hop limit that reports its own exhaustion rather than a wrong nearest. Record a judgement, as an assert or in the head, on whether provenance should also be legible from the row itself or documented as a side table, with the reason. Mutation-sensitive tests covering the one-hop case, a multi-hop case, and the limit-exhausted case. Sequence after the write-boundary request. Publish exact-head artifacts at every changed stable path and obtain independent review with Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions.","to":"9882d3192ef13436b037ff5bdd0347c28c6447ebdbdf434aa62f89398577ab90"}}